Introduction
Stiff-person syndrome (SPS) is a rare ne urological disorder characterized by
muscle stiffness, hyperreﬂexia and elevated serum levels of creatinine kinase.
A key feature in the pathophysiology of SPS is the impairment of GABAergic
neurotransmission [1]. Type 1 diabetes (T1D) results from the destruc-
tion of insulin-producing beta cells in pancreatic islets and leads to metabolic
derangement which can only be compensated by daily injections of exogenous
